WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.253
Lesson five point two.

2
00:00:01.583 --> 00:00:03.953
The nine numbers axis one reads from every

3
00:00:03.953 --> 00:00:04.339
window.

4
00:00:08.313 --> 00:00:10.557
Axis one never takes in a whole song at

5
00:00:10.557 --> 00:00:10.837
once.

6
00:00:11.174 --> 00:00:13.922
It cuts the drums into windows: two bars,

7
00:00:13.922 --> 00:00:16.334
thirty-two sixteenth-note slots, by nine

8
00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.007
drum voices.

9
00:00:17.344 --> 00:00:19.756
Each hit is rounded to its nearest slot,

10
00:00:19.756 --> 00:00:22.055
and whatever was lost in the rounding is

11
00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:22.897
kept beside it.

12
00:00:23.447 --> 00:00:25.152
Here's the window we'll measure.

13
00:00:25.471 --> 00:00:27.815
Kick on beats one and three, snare on two

14
00:00:27.815 --> 00:00:29.946
and four, closed hats on every eighth

15
00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:30.212
note.

16
00:00:30.532 --> 00:00:32.609
It's the battery's own test pattern,

17
00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:35.166
straight rock: exactly the fixed loop from

18
00:00:35.166 --> 00:00:36.338
lesson five point one.

19
00:00:36.895 --> 00:00:39.348
Brightness is velocity: how hard each hit

20
00:00:39.348 --> 00:00:39.505
is.

21
00:00:39.818 --> 00:00:42.010
The pattern sets the kick at a hundred,

22
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.255
the snare at a hundred and ten, the hats

23
00:00:44.255 --> 00:00:46.082
at seventy, out of a hundred and

24
00:00:46.082 --> 00:00:46.760
twenty-seven.

25
00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:49.161
Every hit sits exactly on its grid line.

26
00:00:49.685 --> 00:00:51.855
The nine voices fall into three groups.

27
00:00:52.189 --> 00:00:53.079
Low is the kick.

28
00:00:53.413 --> 00:00:55.416
Mid is the snare and the three toms.

29
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.143
High is the hats, the crash and the ride.

30
00:00:58.477 --> 00:01:00.926
From this one window, axis one takes nine

31
00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:01.371
numbers.

32
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.186
The first four numbers are counts.

33
00:01:06.487 --> 00:01:08.544
Density is simply how many hits a window

34
00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:08.845
holds.

35
00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:11.504
Take the hit grid, H: one where a voice

36
00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.110
hits, nought where it doesn't.

37
00:01:13.411 --> 00:01:15.418
Add it up over every voice, and every

38
00:01:15.418 --> 00:01:15.669
slot.

39
00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.117
Four kicks, four snares, sixteen hats:

40
00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:18.828
twenty-four hits.

41
00:01:19.223 --> 00:01:21.732
Then the same count inside each group, g:

42
00:01:21.732 --> 00:01:23.626
low four, mid four, high sixteen.

43
00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.494
That's numbers one to four: the total, and

44
00:01:26.494 --> 00:01:27.825
the three group densities.

45
00:01:28.278 --> 00:01:30.619
For scale, the middle eighty percent of

46
00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:32.626
the human rock windows hold between

47
00:01:32.626 --> 00:01:34.299
twenty-two and forty-six hits.

48
00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:37.086
A model far busier than that, or one that

49
00:01:37.086 --> 00:01:39.484
never touches a tom, shows up here first.

50
00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.395
Shade the eight beats: the strong slots.

51
00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:46.903
Number five is the share of all hits that

52
00:01:46.903 --> 00:01:47.664
land on a beat.

53
00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.302
Every kick and snare is on a beat: eight.

54
00:01:50.606 --> 00:01:52.382
Half the hats are: eight more.

55
00:01:52.686 --> 00:01:55.020
Sixteen out of twenty-four: nought point

56
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:55.528
six seven.

57
00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:58.606
A warning for the report: the code calls

58
00:01:58.606 --> 00:02:00.827
this weak-to-strong, but what it returns

59
00:02:00.827 --> 00:02:02.170
is the share on the beats.

60
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.649
Describe what it computes, not its name.

61
00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:07.396
Number six is backbeat presence.

62
00:02:07.728 --> 00:02:10.164
Take the mid group's velocity: all the

63
00:02:10.164 --> 00:02:12.102
snare and tom energy in the window.

64
00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.815
Keep the part on beats two and four, and

65
00:02:14.815 --> 00:02:15.922
divide by all of it.

66
00:02:16.623 --> 00:02:18.381
Every snare here is on two or four, at

67
00:02:18.381 --> 00:02:20.354
velocity a hundred and ten: nought point

68
00:02:20.354 --> 00:02:21.426
eight six six of the top.

69
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:22.541
So it's exactly one.

70
00:02:22.798 --> 00:02:24.513
In the funk test pattern, quiet ghost

71
00:02:24.513 --> 00:02:26.100
snares off the beat bring it down to

72
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.172
nought point seven three.

73
00:02:27.429 --> 00:02:29.316
Counting hits alone would give a half;

74
00:02:29.316 --> 00:02:30.988
weighting by velocity lets quiet notes

75
00:02:30.988 --> 00:02:31.631
count for less.

76
00:02:31.888 --> 00:02:33.604
Toms count too, so a fill on the toms

77
00:02:33.604 --> 00:02:34.976
between the backbeats lowers it.

78
00:02:36.164 --> 00:02:38.318
Now scatter the same hits at random: the

79
00:02:38.318 --> 00:02:40.238
battery's matched-density random pattern.

80
00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:42.767
The four counts can't tell the difference:

81
00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.921
still twenty-four, four, four and sixteen.

82
00:02:45.202 --> 00:02:46.981
But the on-beat share falls to nought

83
00:02:46.981 --> 00:02:49.089
point two nine, and backbeat presence to a

84
00:02:49.089 --> 00:02:51.149
quarter: one snare of four landed on a

85
00:02:51.149 --> 00:02:51.945
backbeat by luck.

86
00:02:52.226 --> 00:02:54.053
That's why counts alone are not enough.

87
00:02:57.593 --> 00:03:00.087
Number seven is syncopation: a note on a

88
00:03:00.087 --> 00:03:02.309
weak spot, followed by silence where a

89
00:03:02.309 --> 00:03:03.718
stronger one was expected.

90
00:03:04.044 --> 00:03:06.374
The battery uses Longuet-Higgins and Lee's

91
00:03:06.374 --> 00:03:06.808
measure.

92
00:03:07.689 --> 00:03:09.861
First, squash all nine voices into one

93
00:03:09.861 --> 00:03:12.351
line: a slot is on if anything hits there.

94
00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.917
Each slot gets a metrical weight, how

95
00:03:14.917 --> 00:03:16.186
strong it is in the bar.

96
00:03:16.504 --> 00:03:18.937
Five on the downbeat, four on beat three,

97
00:03:18.937 --> 00:03:21.158
three on beats two and four, two on the

98
00:03:21.158 --> 00:03:23.432
other eighths, and one on the sixteenths

99
00:03:23.432 --> 00:03:24.014
in between.

100
00:03:24.491 --> 00:03:25.095
Now the rule.

101
00:03:25.374 --> 00:03:27.419
For each hit, look one slot ahead, then

102
00:03:27.419 --> 00:03:27.605
two.

103
00:03:27.884 --> 00:03:29.837
If that slot is silent and heavier, the

104
00:03:29.837 --> 00:03:31.836
hit was a push: add the difference in

105
00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:32.161
weight.

106
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.532
Add up every hit in the window, and divide

107
00:03:34.532 --> 00:03:35.787
by thirty, a fixed scale.

108
00:03:36.066 --> 00:03:37.972
The bigger the gap between the weak note

109
00:03:37.972 --> 00:03:39.785
and the strong silence after it, the

110
00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:40.622
stronger the push.

111
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:43.396
In our window, take the hit on slot six,

112
00:03:43.396 --> 00:03:43.961
weight two.

113
00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:46.120
Slot seven is silent, but lighter.

114
00:03:46.428 --> 00:03:48.536
Slot eight is heavier, but it's played.

115
00:03:48.844 --> 00:03:51.106
Every eighth is played, so no hit finds a

116
00:03:51.106 --> 00:03:53.264
heavier silence: syncopation is zero.

117
00:03:54.245 --> 00:03:56.161
Now a different test pattern from the

118
00:03:56.161 --> 00:03:57.774
battery: kick into silence.

119
00:03:58.076 --> 00:04:00.143
A kick on slots nought and seven of each

120
00:04:00.143 --> 00:04:01.353
bar, and nothing else.

121
00:04:01.776 --> 00:04:02.837
Slot seven weighs one.

122
00:04:03.127 --> 00:04:05.346
The next slot, eight, is beat three:

123
00:04:05.346 --> 00:04:06.601
weight four, and silent.

124
00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.434
Four minus one: plus three.

125
00:04:08.724 --> 00:04:09.785
Same again in bar two.

126
00:04:10.075 --> 00:04:12.005
The kicks on the downbeats find nothing

127
00:04:12.005 --> 00:04:12.391
heavier.

128
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.707
Six, over thirty: nought point two.

129
00:04:15.581 --> 00:04:17.760
That's why the rule looks two slots ahead.

130
00:04:18.072 --> 00:04:20.459
Move the kick to slot six: slot seven is

131
00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.846
lighter, so look on to slot eight, silent

132
00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:25.182
and heavier: four minus two, plus two.

133
00:04:25.493 --> 00:04:28.088
Twice, over thirty: nought point one three

134
00:04:28.088 --> 00:04:28.399
three.

135
00:04:29.254 --> 00:04:31.147
But put hats back on every eighth, and

136
00:04:31.147 --> 00:04:33.086
slot eight is no longer silent: zero

137
00:04:33.086 --> 00:04:33.363
again.

138
00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.671
Axis one reads the whole kit as one line,

139
00:04:35.671 --> 00:04:37.564
so it only counts a push the rest of the

140
00:04:37.564 --> 00:04:38.488
kit leaves room for.

141
00:04:38.765 --> 00:04:40.796
In the Groove reference, nearly two human

142
00:04:40.796 --> 00:04:42.412
windows in three read exactly zero.

143
00:04:42.689 --> 00:04:44.720
The scattered random pattern from before,

144
00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.659
full of gaps on the beats, reads nought

145
00:04:46.659 --> 00:04:47.167
point five.

146
00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.426
The last two numbers are about feel.

147
00:04:52.756 --> 00:04:55.062
Velocity spread is the standard deviation

148
00:04:55.062 --> 00:04:56.379
of every hit's velocity.

149
00:04:56.709 --> 00:04:58.850
Take each velocity's distance from the

150
00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:01.430
mean, square it and average, then take the

151
00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.571
square root, to get back to velocity

152
00:05:03.571 --> 00:05:03.901
units.

153
00:05:04.318 --> 00:05:06.036
In our window the mean velocity is

154
00:05:06.036 --> 00:05:07.165
eighty-one point seven.

155
00:05:07.459 --> 00:05:09.324
Kicks sit eighteen above it, snares

156
00:05:09.324 --> 00:05:11.287
twenty-eight above, hats twelve below.

157
00:05:11.582 --> 00:05:13.447
The spread comes out at sixteen point

158
00:05:13.447 --> 00:05:15.459
seven five, which on the nought to one

159
00:05:15.459 --> 00:05:17.226
scale is nought point one three two.

160
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.287
Squaring before averaging means the

161
00:05:19.287 --> 00:05:21.348
snares, furthest from the mean, count

162
00:05:21.348 --> 00:05:21.594
most.

163
00:05:22.403 --> 00:05:24.791
Timing spread is the same calculation over

164
00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.457
each hit's offset: how early or late it is

165
00:05:27.457 --> 00:05:29.901
against its grid line, as a fraction of a

166
00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:30.179
slot.

167
00:05:30.512 --> 00:05:32.956
Every hit here is exactly on the grid, so

168
00:05:32.956 --> 00:05:33.511
it's zero.

169
00:05:33.844 --> 00:05:36.177
The battery's humanised test take, with

170
00:05:36.177 --> 00:05:38.565
the snare pushed late on purpose and every

171
00:05:38.565 --> 00:05:40.898
hit nudged at random, spreads by nought

172
00:05:40.898 --> 00:05:42.730
point nought five five of a slot.

173
00:05:43.064 --> 00:05:45.452
At its hundred and twelve beats per minute

174
00:05:45.452 --> 00:05:47.618
a slot lasts a hundred and thirty-four

175
00:05:47.618 --> 00:05:49.728
milliseconds, so that's about seven

176
00:05:49.728 --> 00:05:50.450
milliseconds.

177
00:05:51.307 --> 00:05:52.170
Here's the catch.

178
00:05:52.474 --> 00:05:54.148
Our drum models output hits only.

179
00:05:54.452 --> 00:05:56.634
The scoring code gives every model hit the

180
00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.663
same velocity and no offset, so every

181
00:05:58.663 --> 00:06:00.895
model window reads zero on both, whatever

182
00:06:00.895 --> 00:06:01.656
the model does.

183
00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.090
Under two percent of the human windows do.

184
00:06:04.395 --> 00:06:06.475
So these two can only ever say not human.

185
00:06:06.779 --> 00:06:08.453
They can't tell our models apart.

186
00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:14.291
In the code the nine are one list, in the

187
00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:15.873
distribution-matching module.

188
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.437
The human reference stores the same nine

189
00:06:18.437 --> 00:06:20.729
numbers for each of its two thousand four

190
00:06:20.729 --> 00:06:22.366
hundred and forty-one windows.

191
00:06:22.693 --> 00:06:25.257
Note the code's names: weak to strong for

192
00:06:25.257 --> 00:06:27.658
the on-beat share, and L H L flat for the

193
00:06:27.658 --> 00:06:28.313
syncopation.

194
00:06:29.286 --> 00:06:31.576
Here are all nine for our window, beside

195
00:06:31.576 --> 00:06:33.493
the middle of the two thousand four

196
00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:35.676
hundred and forty-one human rock windows.

197
00:06:36.081 --> 00:06:38.694
It's sparser than most of the humans: only

198
00:06:38.694 --> 00:06:40.980
about one human window in eight has fewer

199
00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:41.252
hits.

200
00:06:41.578 --> 00:06:43.864
It's more on the beat than nine in ten of

201
00:06:43.864 --> 00:06:44.137
them.

202
00:06:44.463 --> 00:06:46.803
And its velocity is flatter than more than

203
00:06:46.803 --> 00:06:47.892
nine in ten of them.

204
00:06:48.219 --> 00:06:49.525
A loop, not a drummer.

205
00:06:49.979 --> 00:06:51.467
But one window says little.

206
00:06:51.797 --> 00:06:54.111
Axis one compares the whole population of

207
00:06:54.111 --> 00:06:56.204
a model's windows with the humans',

208
00:06:56.204 --> 00:06:57.251
feature by feature.

209
00:06:57.582 --> 00:06:58.849
That's the next lesson.

210
00:07:00.615 --> 00:07:03.051
So every window becomes nine numbers: four

211
00:07:03.051 --> 00:07:05.437
counts, two about placement, one about the

212
00:07:05.437 --> 00:07:07.822
push, and two about feel, which our models

213
00:07:07.822 --> 00:07:08.381
can't play.

214
00:07:08.685 --> 00:07:11.121
Next: how a population of those numbers is

215
00:07:11.121 --> 00:07:12.441
compared with the humans'.

